The size and proportions of a German Shepherd are generally consistent across the breed, with males being larger than females. They stand between 22-26 inches tall at the shoulder and weigh between 70-90 pounds.

Behaviorally, German Shepherds are known for their intelligence, loyalty, and trainability. They are often used as working dogs, including police and military roles, due to their strong drive and ability to learn complex commands. However, they can also make excellent family pets if properly trained and socialized.

