MLLM description: The silky terrier is a small breed with a distinctive long, silky coat that is predominantly light brown or silver-gray in color. Its coat is smooth and shiny, often appearing almost like silk, hence its name. The silky terrier has a compact body with a short, sturdy build. Its head is small with a pointed muzzle, and it has large, expressive eyes that are dark in color. The ears are small and erect, standing upright on top of the head. The silky terrier's tail is long and bushy, often carried over the back.

In terms of size, the silky terrier is typically between 9-12 inches tall at the shoulder and weighs around 7-10 pounds. They have a lively and energetic personality, known for their intelligence and playful nature. Silky terriers are often seen as affectionate companions and are excellent with children. They are also known to be good watchdogs due to their alertness and protective instincts.

